You have fingers.

258
00:09:32,758 --> 00:09:34,034
I like that in a man.

259
00:09:35,310 --> 00:09:38,344
Ah, the American Institute
of Psychical Researchiculating.

260
00:09:39,931 --> 00:09:41,068
Come on into my meat freezer,

261
00:09:41,103 --> 00:09:43,344
I'd like to show you
my research on beefalo.

262
00:09:44,862 --> 00:09:46,620
Should never have bought
that cow dung sprayer.

263
00:09:46,655 --> 00:09:48,344
[Mike chuckles]

264
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:49,965
So you've come back, eh?

265
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,724
After seven years,
you've come back.

266
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:53,103
No, it's not me.

267
00:09:53,137 --> 00:09:54,931
Time has little
meaning in Tibet.

268
00:09:54,965 --> 00:09:56,034
Neither does the
word, Tacorific.

269
00:09:56,068 --> 00:09:57,413
Did my call startle you?

270
00:09:57,448 --> 00:10:00,068
No, I've been expecting
it for seven years.

271
00:10:00,103 --> 00:10:01,413
Well, six and a half.

272
00:10:01,448 --> 00:10:03,379
All of your old students
return, don't they, Professor?

273
00:10:03,413 --> 00:10:05,034
All your ruddy friends
are coming over tonight.

274
00:10:05,068 --> 00:10:06,000
Even the ones you failed.

275
00:10:06,034 --> 00:10:07,793
Particularly
the ones I failed.

276
00:10:07,827 --> 00:10:09,068
They always want
to prove me wrong.

277
00:10:09,103 --> 00:10:11,965
- And I always am wrong.
- And now you.

278
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,206
You want to startle me
and the entire world, eh?

279
00:10:14,241 --> 00:10:16,965
- And I might do just that.
- Boo! Ha ha.

280
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,034
With your help...

281
00:10:19,068 --> 00:10:21,000
I can make
seamless panty hose.

282
00:10:21,034 --> 00:10:23,689
When you called me, I said
I would listen, not help.

283
00:10:23,724 --> 00:10:25,034
Well, he is a psychologist.

284
00:10:25,068 --> 00:10:28,034
As for this
spectacular idea of yours,

285
00:10:28,068 --> 00:10:30,275
it's nothing but Sunday
supplement nonsense.

286
00:10:30,310 --> 00:10:33,586
I mean to invade
the depths of the mind.

287
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:35,000
That is not nonsense.

288
00:10:35,034 --> 00:10:36,655
Excuse me, did
I say, "nonsense"?

289
00:10:36,689 --> 00:10:37,758
I meant fluffer nutter.

290
00:10:37,793 --> 00:10:39,034
I mean idiocy.

291
00:10:39,068 --> 00:10:41,068
Don't condemn me
without a try, Professor.

292
00:10:41,103 --> 00:10:42,344
Too late, you're condemned.

293
00:10:42,379 --> 00:10:45,275
If I succeed, we will
see history unfold itself

294
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:47,758
through the eyes of the subject.

295
00:10:47,793 --> 00:10:49,344
And I know it can be done.

296
00:10:49,379 --> 00:10:50,827
I've seen it.

297
00:10:50,862 --> 00:10:52,689
In the desert huts of
the Shamans of Kassa.

298
00:10:52,724 --> 00:10:53,965
And in Des Moines.

299
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:54,965
And where will you
find a subject weak

300
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,103
and impressionable
enough to arrive

301
00:10:56,137 --> 00:10:57,758
in the required depth of trance?

302
00:10:57,793 --> 00:11:00,137
- They're around.
- Diana...

303
00:11:00,172 --> 00:11:03,931
I'm recombining
DNA, if you don't mind.

304
00:11:03,965 --> 00:11:05,862
What's her full name?
[Servo imitates creaking]

305
00:11:05,896 --> 00:11:07,068
Who knows?

306
00:11:07,103 --> 00:11:09,275
She calls herself Diana Love.

307
00:11:09,310 --> 00:11:11,068
But her real
name is Dynamite.

308
00:11:11,103 --> 00:11:13,482
Don't be afraid, my dear,
no one's going to hurt you.

309
00:11:13,517 --> 00:11:16,068
I'm not afraid of
you, or anybody else.

310
00:11:16,103 --> 00:11:17,965
We'll be with you
in a moment, Diana.

311
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:18,965
Where did you find her?

312
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,724
What does it matter?

313
00:11:20,758 --> 00:11:22,379
You took her off
the street tonight?

314
00:11:22,413 --> 00:11:25,000
[Servo sings nonchalantly]
You unmitigated fool.

315
00:11:25,034 --> 00:11:26,413
- Am I?
- Ah, his blush.

316
00:11:26,448 --> 00:11:28,034
Her type is the
most easily influenced

317
00:11:28,068 --> 00:11:29,689
in basic character groups.

318
00:11:29,724 --> 00:11:31,137
Almost devoid of willpower.

319
00:11:31,172 --> 00:11:33,586
That's why I chose
one of her class.

320
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:34,724
Has she agreed to this?

321
00:11:34,758 --> 00:11:36,517
I'm paying her well,

322
00:11:36,551 --> 00:11:39,965
although I dare say she has no
idea what I'm paying her for.

323
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,275
I will not help you, Quintus.

324
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:43,379
Then I'll do it
alone, without your help.

325
00:11:43,413 --> 00:11:45,551
Don't you want to
protect her, Professor?

326
00:11:45,586 --> 00:11:48,068
- Don't you have any Proust?
- From me?

327
00:11:49,517 --> 00:11:50,620
It'll take too long.

328
00:11:51,482 --> 00:11:53,275
Weeks.
48 hours.

329
00:11:53,310 --> 00:11:54,310
Impossible.

330
00:11:54,344 --> 00:11:55,965
Instead of repeated sessions,

331
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,344
I'll keep her under
the full two days.

332
00:11:58,379 --> 00:12:00,379
I won't even wake her up to eat.

333
00:12:00,413 --> 00:12:03,310
Instead, I'll direct all
her needs within the trance.

334
00:12:03,344 --> 00:12:05,413
- That could prove fatal.
- Why thank you.

335
00:12:05,448 --> 00:12:09,034
No, not with you
watching, Doctor.

336
00:12:09,068 --> 00:12:11,310
I see I have no
choice in the matter.

337
00:12:11,344 --> 00:12:12,965
A scientist with
a deep knife scar.

338
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,172
We'll be remembered for this.

339
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:17,103
I hope it will
not be as murderers.

340
00:12:17,137 --> 00:12:19,275
Oh, you can kill me,
that's okay, I don't care.

341
00:12:21,241 --> 00:12:22,379
Say, how much
longer am I gonna

342
00:12:22,413 --> 00:12:24,655
have to stay in
this crummy joint?

343
00:12:24,689 --> 00:12:27,655
Two days, perhaps longer.

344
00:12:27,689 --> 00:12:28,793
Two years later...

345
00:12:29,689 --> 00:12:30,896
Do you have to do all that?

346
00:12:30,931 --> 00:12:32,275
Take it easy, Diana.

347
00:12:32,310 --> 00:12:33,793
Don't let the sound of your
own wheels drive you crazy.

348
00:12:33,827 --> 00:12:35,551
Are you subject
to fainting spells?

349
00:12:35,586 --> 00:12:37,241
Hey, he has a Ben
Franklin ice auger.

350
00:12:37,275 --> 00:12:39,448
Do you have any difficulty
getting up in the morning?

351
00:12:39,482 --> 00:12:41,000
[Crow moans and grunts]
[Diana chuckles]

352
00:12:41,034 --> 00:12:41,724
I don't.

353
00:12:42,793 --> 00:12:44,379
- I get up in the afternoon.
- Felix.

354
00:12:45,413 --> 00:12:46,586
That's easy.

355
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:47,344
I think you'll live.

356
00:12:47,379 --> 00:12:49,689
Unless loser here, kills you.

357
00:12:52,448 --> 00:12:54,000
Your witness.

358
00:12:55,068 --> 00:12:58,034
Dirty, greasy walls,
a short-lived design fad.

359
00:12:58,068 --> 00:13:00,931
I don't think I
wanna be hypnotized.

360
00:13:00,965 --> 00:13:02,862
You're being paid $500.

361
00:13:02,896 --> 00:13:04,034
That's a lot
of money back now.

362
00:13:04,068 --> 00:13:05,034
I think it might
be better if you

363
00:13:05,068 --> 00:13:07,413
took off that heavy bracelet.

364
00:13:07,448 --> 00:13:08,482
No, thanks.

365
00:13:08,517 --> 00:13:10,689
I'll just keep it,
if you don't mind.

366
00:13:10,724 --> 00:13:12,034
Very well.

367
00:13:12,068 --> 00:13:14,379
Say, friend, tell her a
penny saved is a penny earned.

368
00:13:16,103 --> 00:13:17,620
Do you see my hand?

369
00:13:17,655 --> 00:13:19,241
Do you think I'm Dale?

370
00:13:19,275 --> 00:13:22,068
There is no end
to my hand, is there?

371
00:13:22,103 --> 00:13:24,034
No, I guess I'm
not getting it, sorry.

372
00:13:24,068 --> 00:13:26,103
You can always
take another turn.

373
00:13:26,137 --> 00:13:28,413
Oh, and by the way, sleep!

374
00:13:30,310 --> 00:13:31,724
Around the knuckle...

375
00:13:31,758 --> 00:13:33,000
Over the gums.

376
00:13:33,034 --> 00:13:34,103
Over the finger.

377
00:13:34,137 --> 00:13:35,517
Look out, stomach,
here it comes.

378
00:13:35,551 --> 00:13:37,586
Like riding a tiny
roller coaster, isn't it?

379
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:40,068
In that I feel like
throwing up on you?

380
00:13:40,103 --> 00:13:41,655
- Yes...
- Yes.

381
00:13:42,310 --> 00:13:43,931
Yes, yes.
You're riding.

382
00:13:43,965 --> 00:13:45,379
- And now, sleep!
- Whoa!

383
00:13:46,758 --> 00:13:47,689
First slowly...

384
00:13:47,724 --> 00:13:49,137
Then fastly.

385
00:13:50,344 --> 00:13:51,482
- Then faster.
- Give me liberty,

386
00:13:51,517 --> 00:13:54,931
or give me, oh no
wait, that's Pat Henry.

387
00:13:54,965 --> 00:13:56,275
Around...

388
00:13:56,310 --> 00:13:58,724
- Do you like my lip liner?
- Around,

389
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,068
and around.

390
00:14:01,103 --> 00:14:02,206
He's not hypnotizing her,

391
00:14:02,241 --> 00:14:04,172
- he's merely boring her.
- Silent.

392
00:14:05,862 --> 00:14:08,931
- Silent.
- He's hypnotized himself.

393
00:14:08,965 --> 00:14:09,655
Silent.

394
00:14:10,586 --> 00:14:13,068
[group imitates spooky music]

395
00:14:13,103 --> 00:14:15,034
Five years later...
[group chuckles]

396
00:14:15,068 --> 00:14:17,965
And the silence is
deeper, and deeper.

397
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,034
[group imitates spooky music]

398
00:14:20,068 --> 00:14:21,206
Like a well.

399
00:14:22,034 --> 00:14:24,827
Like a deep, deep well.

400
00:14:24,862 --> 00:14:26,103
Like a circle in a spiral.

401
00:14:26,137 --> 00:14:27,034
Like falling.

402
00:14:27,068 --> 00:14:28,827
Like a wheel within a wheel.

403
00:14:28,862 --> 00:14:29,862
Falling...

404
00:14:31,034 --> 00:14:33,000
- Into a deep...
- Cleansing.

405
00:14:33,034 --> 00:14:34,172
- Discount.
- Deep...

406
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:35,448
- Heating.
- Purple!

407
00:14:35,482 --> 00:14:38,137
Sleep.
[group imitates snoring]

408
00:14:38,172 --> 00:14:42,137
We are in a dark silence,
and we breathe in water.

409
00:14:43,482 --> 00:14:44,448
We are one.

410
00:14:44,482 --> 00:14:45,758
You know, early
to bed, early to rise

411
00:14:45,793 --> 00:14:49,172
makes a man healthy,
wealthy and wise, no?

412
00:14:50,241 --> 00:14:52,827
- When I touch you...
- I think about myself.

413
00:14:52,862 --> 00:14:54,482
No, no, no, wait, that's wrong.

414
00:14:54,517 --> 00:14:55,379
We will be one.

415
00:14:55,413 --> 00:14:57,034
We'll be me, for
convenience sake.

416
00:14:57,068 --> 00:15:02,172
[Mystery Science Theater
3000 theme music]

417
00:15:04,827 --> 00:15:06,413
You're going back farther.

418
00:15:08,103 --> 00:15:09,310
Going back...

419
00:15:09,344 --> 00:15:12,206
Back, back, oh, I snagged
it on the warning track!

420
00:15:13,724 --> 00:15:15,206
It is another time.

421
00:15:16,068 --> 00:15:19,551
Must not look at
Mister Weatherbee.

422
00:15:20,896 --> 00:15:23,758
- Farther...
- I've always loathed pencils.

423
00:15:26,068 --> 00:15:27,206
And when you wake up, I'll be

424
00:15:27,241 --> 00:15:29,103
the foxiest guy
you've ever seen.

425
00:15:29,137 --> 00:15:30,034
What are you doing?

426
00:15:30,068 --> 00:15:31,206
She can't possibly hear you.

427
00:15:32,586 --> 00:15:33,827
Can we roll her
out in the hall?

428
00:15:33,862 --> 00:15:35,344
I've got other clients.

429
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:40,586
No, I am nowhere.

430
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:41,758
Oh, Nebraska.

431
00:15:42,793 --> 00:15:45,758
- But I exist.
- My glasses popped on!

432
00:15:45,793 --> 00:15:49,275
You may speak.
[Crow imitates barking]

433
00:15:49,310 --> 00:15:50,517
Do you hear me?

434
00:15:52,413 --> 00:15:53,344
Oui.

435
00:15:53,379 --> 00:15:56,034
Are family, I've
got all my sis...

436
00:15:56,068 --> 00:15:57,379
What do you see?

437
00:15:57,413 --> 00:15:59,000
[Diana speaks French]

438
00:15:59,034 --> 00:16:02,517
Tish! That's French!
[imitates kissing]

439
00:16:02,551 --> 00:16:05,172
I will no longer
shower or shave my legs.

440
00:16:06,379 --> 00:16:08,517
And I hate all Americans now.

441
00:16:11,137 --> 00:16:13,482
Well, it's happened.

442
00:16:13,517 --> 00:16:15,758
Something about a
hat, that's all I got.

443
00:16:15,793 --> 00:16:17,827
You've broken into the past.

444
00:16:17,862 --> 00:16:18,965
Yes.

445
00:16:20,068 --> 00:16:21,517
Yes, I have.

446
00:16:23,103 --> 00:16:24,827
Yes, it's the 23rd
hour of our telethon,

447
00:16:24,862 --> 00:16:26,206
and we're going all the way.

448
00:16:27,068 --> 00:16:29,034
Now the real work will begin.

449
00:16:29,068 --> 00:16:30,275
What more is there to do?

450
00:16:30,310 --> 00:16:32,379
Well, the wall,
for one thing.

451
00:16:32,413 --> 00:16:34,586
So you were French once.

452
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:35,793
And of nobility.

453
00:16:37,310 --> 00:16:39,448
You see it all too
dimly, don't you, Diana?

454
00:16:39,482 --> 00:16:41,034
Yes, through a
glass darkly, yeah.

455
00:16:41,068 --> 00:16:42,344
Too dimly.

456
00:16:43,310 --> 00:16:45,448
- Well, my dear...
- I don't give a damn.

457
00:16:45,482 --> 00:16:48,586
You will find that
there are other times,

458
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:49,827
and other lives.

459
00:16:51,379 --> 00:16:53,862
Soon you will find
one that I may visit.

460
00:16:53,896 --> 00:16:55,655
Although I have been
barred from most times

461
00:16:55,689 --> 00:16:58,000
'cause of my unpaid
parking tickets.

462
00:16:58,034 --> 00:16:59,344
Come on, open
the hangar door...

463
00:16:59,379 --> 00:17:00,655
[imitates airplane engine]
That's a good girl.

464
00:17:00,689 --> 00:17:02,344
Research has
shown that my lap

465
00:17:02,379 --> 00:17:04,310
is the best place for her.

466
00:17:06,137 --> 00:17:09,379
I, I have no
heartbeat, oh, my G...

467
00:17:11,758 --> 00:17:14,827
She's all the way back
to Quest For Fire time.

468
00:17:14,862 --> 00:17:18,241
[grunts]

469
00:17:19,413 --> 00:17:20,586
Oh, why do I do this?

470
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:23,275
I hypnotize all day,
then I go home to a cat.

471
00:17:24,758 --> 00:17:27,103
It's Must See TV
night, I have to get home!

472
00:17:27,137 --> 00:17:28,517
You told her nothing?

473
00:17:29,103 --> 00:17:30,827
You asked her nothing?

474
00:17:30,862 --> 00:17:32,034
Watch carefully.

475
00:17:32,068 --> 00:17:35,034
Your watching's been
pretty lax, these days.

476
00:17:35,068 --> 00:17:36,241
It's started.

477
00:17:36,965 --> 00:17:38,068
She's going.

478
00:17:38,103 --> 00:17:40,103
Oh, I'm puffy, I'm so puffy.

479
00:17:40,137 --> 00:17:42,379
I'm retaining
water in my wrists.

480
00:17:42,413 --> 00:17:43,931
Why'd you bring
her sewing kit?

481
00:17:43,965 --> 00:17:47,517
Dinosaur is trying to
take my charm bracelet, I...

482
00:17:51,206 --> 00:17:53,793
Slightly Risky Liasons.

483
00:17:53,827 --> 00:17:56,586
She's in the gorilla exhibit
at the Lincoln Park Zoo.

484
00:17:57,931 --> 00:17:59,827
- Sir Ray Nitschke.
- Ew.

485
00:17:59,862 --> 00:18:03,000
- How fares the witch?
- Real, real nice, thanks.

486
00:18:03,034 --> 00:18:05,448
Do you fear me, Sorceress?

487
00:18:05,482 --> 00:18:07,137
Why, Gobbo's the gentlest jailer

488
00:18:07,172 --> 00:18:09,034
ever to gouge a prisoner's eye.

489
00:18:09,068 --> 00:18:10,586
You wanna run
that by me again?

490
00:18:12,241 --> 00:18:13,758
Keep thee from me!

491
00:18:13,793 --> 00:18:15,172
Fret me not, hell hag.

492
00:18:15,206 --> 00:18:16,344
Miss Hell Hag.

493
00:18:16,379 --> 00:18:17,620
You've lost your
powers as tomorrow

494
00:18:17,655 --> 00:18:19,103
you shall lose your head
upon the chopping block!

495
00:18:19,137 --> 00:18:21,034
- Chubby block?
- My head?

496
00:18:21,068 --> 00:18:22,241
I shall lose my head?

497
00:18:22,275 --> 00:18:23,827
Uh, you're
singing your hair...

498
00:18:23,862 --> 00:18:25,000
[group chuckles]

499
00:18:25,034 --> 00:18:27,000
Has your brain recoiled
from it and forgotten?

500
00:18:27,034 --> 00:18:28,068
Aye, you shall lose it,

501
00:18:28,103 --> 00:18:29,793
and it will roll like a melon,

502
00:18:29,827 --> 00:18:31,068
and you'll be clutching
it to your bosom

503
00:18:31,103 --> 00:18:32,793
when they bury you
at the crossroads,

504
00:18:32,827 --> 00:18:35,068
a stake through
your black heart.

505
00:18:35,103 --> 00:18:36,827
- Ew!
- Yes, I remember.

506
00:18:37,551 --> 00:18:38,620
They said I was a witch.

507
00:18:38,655 --> 00:18:40,000
She has a
Flashdance look going.

508
00:18:40,034 --> 00:18:41,137
- Yeah.
- But it's a lie,

509
00:18:41,172 --> 00:18:42,275
a terrible lie,
I am not a witch.

510
00:18:42,310 --> 00:18:43,206
You must believe me!

511
00:18:43,241 --> 00:18:44,482
But I believe it!

512
00:18:45,241 --> 00:18:46,344
Look on me.

513
00:18:46,379 --> 00:18:47,379
He's an attractive
prison matron.

514
00:18:47,413 --> 00:18:48,931
Am I not ugly?

515
00:18:48,965 --> 00:18:51,758
Am I not the rancid
