765
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:08,172
I'm heading to Rivendell.

766
00:28:08,206 --> 00:28:09,965
Would you climb the
very walls of the tower?

767
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:12,000
If I found no
other course, yes.

768
00:28:12,034 --> 00:28:13,965
Wouldst thou
eatest a jar of bugs?

769
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:16,862
Wouldst that I had a
love as great as thine.

770
00:28:16,896 --> 00:28:18,206
What arts thou
supported with, Livia?

771
00:28:18,241 --> 00:28:19,758
Where do you
journey, this night?

772
00:28:19,793 --> 00:28:20,620
To the cemetery.

773
00:28:21,689 --> 00:28:23,310
I must speak with
the digger Smolkin.

774
00:28:23,344 --> 00:28:24,310
Slab-o-face.

775
00:28:24,344 --> 00:28:26,896
They convicted Helene
of bewitching him.

776
00:28:26,931 --> 00:28:29,448
- I believe it not.
- Nor I.

777
00:28:29,482 --> 00:28:33,172
Go, seek poor Smolkin and bring
the proof to free thy love.

778
00:28:33,206 --> 00:28:34,517
Thank you, Livia.

779
00:28:34,551 --> 00:28:35,862
Good night.

780
00:28:35,896 --> 00:28:38,655
Take care, 'tis the eve
of the witch's Sabbath.

781
00:28:38,689 --> 00:28:40,931
So, fare thee well and stuff.

782
00:28:44,068 --> 00:28:44,965
Oh!

783
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,586
Ow, that one hurt
for some reason.

784
00:28:48,965 --> 00:28:49,931
- His nose grew!
- The needle

785
00:28:49,965 --> 00:28:52,000
of my compass swings to north.

786
00:28:52,034 --> 00:28:54,862
'Tis whimpering Helene I put
in prison for the axe to kiss.

787
00:28:54,896 --> 00:28:56,344
Yeah, kiss my axe.

788
00:28:56,379 --> 00:28:58,413
Next, we'll meet
Pendragon at his tavern home.

789
00:28:59,827 --> 00:29:02,000
'Ere this night is done,
I'll have his heart,

790
00:29:02,034 --> 00:29:04,758
or else I'll have his soul.

791
00:29:04,793 --> 00:29:07,068
I feel delighted
in a generic way.

792
00:29:08,103 --> 00:29:10,103
Ah, Weekend at
Bernies, the early years.

793
00:29:10,137 --> 00:29:12,379
This is how Anthony
Quinn's wife must feel.

794
00:29:12,413 --> 00:29:13,620
[group chuckles]

795
00:29:15,137 --> 00:29:17,034
Ah, the medieval Squiggy.

796
00:29:17,068 --> 00:29:18,827
Let's see, what
rhymes with coffin?

797
00:29:18,862 --> 00:29:21,310
Hoffin, Soften,
John McLaughlin...

798
00:29:21,344 --> 00:29:24,000
He also does puppet
shows with the corpses.

799
00:29:25,862 --> 00:29:26,896
Arthur's keeper,

800
00:29:27,965 --> 00:29:31,103
I would have a room for
my mouldering friend.

801
00:29:31,137 --> 00:29:33,068
Are you the digger Smolkin?

802
00:29:33,103 --> 00:29:35,275
I've been told
that I am Smolkin,

803
00:29:35,310 --> 00:29:38,103
but I am mad so cannot
be sure of anything.

804
00:29:38,137 --> 00:29:39,655
Then how can you
be sure you're mad?

805
00:29:40,827 --> 00:29:41,965
You are bewitched?

806
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,827
- Terribly.
- Bothered? Bewildered?

807
00:29:43,862 --> 00:29:46,655
Well tell me,
Smolkin, I must know.

808
00:29:46,689 --> 00:29:48,275
Was it Helene who did it to you?

809
00:29:48,310 --> 00:29:51,793
Helene, who must suffer
death for thy enchantment?

810
00:29:51,827 --> 00:29:54,793
Being enchanted, I
have no way of knowing.

811
00:29:54,827 --> 00:29:57,172
They say the enchantment
has destroyed my reason.

812
00:29:57,206 --> 00:29:58,551
- That's a face.
- Without reason,

813
00:29:58,586 --> 00:30:00,103
there is no memory.

814
00:30:00,137 --> 00:30:02,689
So it must follow
that I do not remember

815
00:30:02,724 --> 00:30:04,689
who it was who bewitched me.

816
00:30:04,724 --> 00:30:06,620
Do you jest with
me, grave digger?

817
00:30:06,655 --> 00:30:08,137
Again, I cannot say.

818
00:30:08,172 --> 00:30:12,241
I am mad, so therefore cannot
tell a jest from a joust.

819
00:30:12,275 --> 00:30:14,068
Dig's graves and
plays with your mind.

820
00:30:14,103 --> 00:30:15,689
I have much to do this night.

821
00:30:15,724 --> 00:30:17,068
Gotta help
Strider move a couch.

822
00:30:17,103 --> 00:30:19,724
I don't think thou
art as mad as all say.

823
00:30:19,758 --> 00:30:21,034
Come on, Huggie,
what do you know?

824
00:30:21,068 --> 00:30:22,551
Stir up thy brain, Smolkin.

825
00:30:23,862 --> 00:30:26,310
I'll be back to ask more of you.

826
00:30:26,344 --> 00:30:28,689
Again, I cannot say
if you will be back

827
00:30:28,724 --> 00:30:29,931
for I am mad.

828
00:30:29,965 --> 00:30:32,413
And wouldst thou pick
me up a MAD Magazine?

829
00:30:32,448 --> 00:30:35,724
I have to watch
Mad About You tonight.

830
00:30:35,758 --> 00:30:37,689
Madness is just
a cry for help.

831
00:30:37,724 --> 00:30:40,724
Ah, well, back to work.

832
00:30:40,758 --> 00:30:42,620
And back to my
Tin Pan Alley songs.

833
00:30:42,655 --> 00:30:44,103
♪ Dickety, dickety horse

834
00:30:44,137 --> 00:30:47,068
- Oh, cripes.
- ♪ My guest is dead, of course

835
00:30:47,103 --> 00:30:50,379
- ♪ The clock struck two
- Central time.

836
00:30:50,413 --> 00:30:54,517
- ♪ He's turning blue
- And I'm Hindu Babaloo,

837
00:30:54,551 --> 00:30:57,068
Dippity do, yadda, hoona, hey.
[Servo laughs]

838
00:30:57,103 --> 00:30:59,793
♪ With little or no remorse

839
00:30:59,827 --> 00:31:01,000
Oh, that was pretty weak.

840
00:31:01,034 --> 00:31:02,206
Yeah, it didn't
quite scan, did it?

841
00:31:02,241 --> 00:31:05,310
[Helene cries]
[bangs on coffin]

842
00:31:05,344 --> 00:31:07,586
Hey, something actually
stopped him from singing.

843
00:31:07,620 --> 00:31:08,517
Yay!

844
00:31:09,068 --> 00:31:10,241
Nice.

845
00:31:10,275 --> 00:31:12,689
Apparently there were Hardware
Hanks in the middle ages.

846
00:31:12,724 --> 00:31:15,896
Gettest thou a cemetery
full of savings, at Menards!

847
00:31:15,931 --> 00:31:18,034
[Helene cries out]

848
00:31:18,068 --> 00:31:20,137
Uh, you could help me
from the inside, you know.

849
00:31:21,206 --> 00:31:24,344
[Helene gasps]
Soft, girl, soft.

850
00:31:24,379 --> 00:31:26,379
- I'll say.
- Thou art safe.

851
00:31:26,413 --> 00:31:30,000
What grisly monster
closed you in this box?

852
00:31:30,034 --> 00:31:31,862
- Whoa, don't do that!
- Was it I?

853
00:31:31,896 --> 00:31:33,931
Help me, for
God's sake, help me.

854
00:31:33,965 --> 00:31:35,827
Aye, that I will,
though my entangled brain

855
00:31:35,862 --> 00:31:38,068
could bring thee
more harm than help.

856
00:31:38,931 --> 00:31:40,034
Do I know thee?

857
00:31:40,068 --> 00:31:41,620
Weren't we in
homeroom together?

858
00:31:41,655 --> 00:31:42,862
Yes, yes, I do.

859
00:31:42,896 --> 00:31:45,931
Thou art Helene, who
cast a spell on me!

860
00:31:45,965 --> 00:31:48,310
Spell?
Nay, not I.

861
00:31:48,344 --> 00:31:50,965
If you are Smolkin then you know
we have never met before.

862
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:53,068
If I am Smolkin.

863
00:31:53,103 --> 00:31:54,517
I may be James Coco.

864
00:31:54,551 --> 00:31:57,137
- Come, out of this rot.
- And into my rot.

865
00:31:57,172 --> 00:31:59,068
And tell me what I may do.

866
00:31:59,103 --> 00:32:00,827
Anyone gonna bury
me some time soon?

867
00:32:00,862 --> 00:32:02,034
Oh, I beg you.

868
00:32:02,517 --> 00:32:03,655
Hide me, please.

869
00:32:03,689 --> 00:32:06,206
Get me to a place that
I may stay the night.

870
00:32:06,241 --> 00:32:08,931
At 12 the witch's
Sabbath will occur.

871
00:32:08,965 --> 00:32:10,482
At dawn, they will execute

872
00:32:10,517 --> 00:32:12,655
the three witches
condemned by law.

873
00:32:12,689 --> 00:32:14,724
Oh, if I may but live
to see the sunrise,

874
00:32:14,758 --> 00:32:17,172
I shall have a whole year
to prove my innocence.

875
00:32:17,206 --> 00:32:18,827
These laws are
positively medieval.

876
00:32:18,862 --> 00:32:20,000
Aye, the witch's Sabbath.

877
00:32:20,034 --> 00:32:22,034
It will be held this
very night, here,

878
00:32:22,068 --> 00:32:24,689
in mine own cherished cemetery.

879
00:32:24,724 --> 00:32:26,655
Go, into the mutton cart.

880
00:32:26,689 --> 00:32:27,862
I'll take thee to a place

881
00:32:27,896 --> 00:32:30,896
where none save Satan
himself might find thee.

882
00:32:30,931 --> 00:32:32,724
His head looks
like a sand trap.

883
00:32:32,758 --> 00:32:34,413
Lie still, old man.

884
00:32:35,275 --> 00:32:37,172
I'll make thy bed when I return.

885
00:32:37,206 --> 00:32:38,862
And I'll leave
a light on for you.

886
00:32:38,896 --> 00:32:41,103
[Servo hums]
[cat meows]

887
00:32:42,724 --> 00:32:43,724
Meow.

888
00:32:44,793 --> 00:32:46,000
Me, wow.

889
00:32:46,034 --> 00:32:47,620
Ah, she still coughs
up hairballs, though.

890
00:32:47,655 --> 00:32:50,000
I'd like to flea bomb
her, I'll tell you that.

891
00:32:50,034 --> 00:32:51,241
Hey, hey.

892
00:32:52,862 --> 00:32:54,034
Hey, she's got a zipper.

893
00:32:54,068 --> 00:32:55,310
Weren't those invented--

894
00:32:55,344 --> 00:32:57,724
If she wants a zipper,
she can have a zipper, Mike.

895
00:32:57,758 --> 00:32:59,206
- Ow!
- Hee hee.

896
00:33:00,758 --> 00:33:01,551
Good evening, Livia.

897
00:33:02,482 --> 00:33:03,827
Welcome to the Gabriel's Horn.

898
00:33:03,862 --> 00:33:05,000
- Sorry, we're full.
- Join me,

899
00:33:05,034 --> 00:33:06,310
Scroop, and rest
thy meaty burden.

900
00:33:06,344 --> 00:33:08,034
All staff'll
be down in a sec.

901
00:33:08,068 --> 00:33:09,310
I see you are prepared.

902
00:33:09,344 --> 00:33:12,758
Corn flowers, wolfsbane,
chicken bones.

903
00:33:12,793 --> 00:33:14,689
Snakes, frogs and amulets.

904
00:33:14,724 --> 00:33:15,931
Big screen TV.

905
00:33:15,965 --> 00:33:18,241
No witch will pass
my door, this night.

906
00:33:18,275 --> 00:33:20,965
And here's garlic,
best protection of all.

907
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:22,551
Hate it when the
waiter sits down with you.

908
00:33:22,586 --> 00:33:23,965
If there's one who
can handle witches

909
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:25,862
- and the imps that serve them,
- Oh, boy.

910
00:33:25,896 --> 00:33:27,862
It's Scroop of
the Gabriel's Horn.

911
00:33:27,896 --> 00:33:29,034
We can't all be clever.

912
00:33:29,068 --> 00:33:30,172
And don't feed your
imp from the table,

913
00:33:30,206 --> 00:33:31,620
he won't go back to
his regular food.

914
00:33:31,655 --> 00:33:33,931
- Scroop, bring some ale.
- Rest thy corpulence.

915
00:33:33,965 --> 00:33:35,034
I'll take the ale.

916
00:33:35,068 --> 00:33:37,103
I'm not corpulent,
I'm big boned.

917
00:33:38,068 --> 00:33:40,206
Digger Smolkin says,
"Eatest mine dust."

918
00:33:40,241 --> 00:33:41,413
It seems like a nice night,

919
00:33:41,448 --> 00:33:43,827
but I do not know for I am mad.

920
00:33:44,862 --> 00:33:46,862
I call it Bowling
Ball in Repose.

921
00:33:50,379 --> 00:33:53,551
This movie's like
a medieval Ghost, huh?

922
00:33:53,586 --> 00:33:54,931
Thank you, Scroop.

923
00:33:54,965 --> 00:33:56,827
You can leave the
ale on the table.

924
00:33:56,862 --> 00:33:59,000
Has Adam come with the
chaps to prison quarters?

925
00:33:59,034 --> 00:34:01,206
So they had filthy
walls back then, too?

926
00:34:02,689 --> 00:34:03,827
No, I am not she.

927
00:34:04,862 --> 00:34:06,275
Forgive the look
on my face, Livia.

928
00:34:06,310 --> 00:34:07,655
I'm just butt-ugly.

929
00:34:07,689 --> 00:34:10,724
- For a moment, I-
- Be not ashamed of love.

930
00:34:10,758 --> 00:34:13,275
Please, I have to finish
my sculpture of Eisenhower.

931
00:34:14,827 --> 00:34:16,034
My thanks for
bringing the ale.

932
00:34:16,068 --> 00:34:17,448
That's a nice skort on.

933
00:34:17,482 --> 00:34:18,482
Your drink could
bring but only

934
00:34:18,517 --> 00:34:21,068
half the forgetfulness you seek.

935
00:34:21,103 --> 00:34:22,586
And what of the other half?

936
00:34:23,793 --> 00:34:24,896
Look to me for it.

937
00:34:26,379 --> 00:34:28,827
Mmm, her breath
smells like Fancy Feast.

938
00:34:30,931 --> 00:34:32,275
Ooh, you're tongue
is like sandpaper.

939
00:34:32,310 --> 00:34:33,793
I can only presume
that you have, by that,

940
00:34:33,827 --> 00:34:36,034
released some violence
that has inflamed thee.

941
00:34:36,068 --> 00:34:37,034
Speaking of inflamed...

942
00:34:37,068 --> 00:34:38,655
For years.

943
00:34:38,689 --> 00:34:41,000
I would not bring the truth
of it before thee now, if...

944
00:34:41,034 --> 00:34:42,379
Now-eth?
[group chuckles]

945
00:34:42,413 --> 00:34:45,137
If that Helene were
not as good as dead.

946
00:34:45,172 --> 00:34:46,931
As good as dead
is not dead, Livia.

947
00:34:46,965 --> 00:34:48,206
But she will be, let's rock.

948
00:34:48,241 --> 00:34:51,068
The first light of morning,
she will be lost to you.

949
00:34:51,103 --> 00:34:52,241
Wow, eager gal.

950
00:34:52,275 --> 00:34:53,517
Our spirits may
despair, Pendragon,

951
00:34:53,551 --> 00:34:56,551
but dare those spirits
tie the hands of flesh?

952
00:34:56,586 --> 00:34:59,862
- Do not tempt me.
- I do not tempt, I give.

953
00:34:59,896 --> 00:35:01,586
She's perky, I
like her attitude.

954
00:35:01,620 --> 00:35:06,448
[Mystery Science Theater
3000 theme music]

955
00:35:08,793 --> 00:35:09,862
Where have you brought me?

956
00:35:09,896 --> 00:35:11,551
The deepest
part of the forest.

957
00:35:11,586 --> 00:35:13,793
Go you through the brambles
till you see a light.

958
00:35:13,827 --> 00:35:15,896
There you will find
a house and hearth.

959
00:35:15,931 --> 00:35:17,034
A house?

960
00:35:17,068 --> 00:35:18,827
Will I be safe there?

961
00:35:18,862 --> 00:35:20,793
A madman can't
be sure of that.

962
00:35:20,827 --> 00:35:23,482
No more than whether you
bewitched me, or did not.

963
00:35:23,517 --> 00:35:25,448
Oh, sure, throw that at me.

964
00:35:25,482 --> 00:35:27,862
♪ Hey, diddle diddle,
the rat and the fiddle

965
00:35:27,896 --> 00:35:28,931
Oh...

966
00:35:28,965 --> 00:35:30,482
♪ The corpse jumped
over his tomb

967
00:35:30,517 --> 00:35:31,827
Now that's purely gratuitous.

968
00:35:31,862 --> 00:35:33,379
That stinks.
[frog croaks]

969
00:35:36,137 --> 00:35:38,862
That frog's a
good licking size.

970
00:35:38,896 --> 00:35:40,000
[Helene cries out]

971
00:35:40,034 --> 00:35:42,172
A small, amphibious
reptile, run!

972
00:35:43,137 --> 00:35:45,379
Hey, there's smudge
in the orange grove.

973
00:35:46,689 --> 00:35:47,793
Ah, it's noon.

974
00:35:47,827 --> 00:35:51,310
Corman's theory of
directing, light, and get away.

975
00:35:51,344 --> 00:35:53,068
Hey, that leather
mug salesman's

976
00:35:53,103 --> 00:35:54,896
doing all right for himself.

977
00:35:56,862 --> 00:35:58,241
What a pretty yamaka.

978
00:35:59,862 --> 00:36:02,896
Grumpy, Grump, Sneezy,
let me in, it's Snow!

979
00:36:04,862 --> 00:36:06,310
James Woods.
[Helene screams]

980
00:36:07,758 --> 00:36:09,724
- I don't like tudor houses!
- Enough of this.

981
00:36:09,758 --> 00:36:11,275
I demand you bring
her out of it, now.

982
00:36:11,310 --> 00:36:12,413
No, Professor...

983
00:36:12,448 --> 00:36:13,620
- Is he sitting on her?
- I don't know

984
00:36:13,655 --> 00:36:14,724
what's being done
to her, right now,

985
00:36:14,758 --> 00:36:16,379
but the shock of
returning might kill her.

986
00:36:16,413 --> 00:36:18,103
We may already
have done that.

987
00:36:18,137 --> 00:36:20,758
But enough of us,
back to our film.

988
00:36:20,793 --> 00:36:22,241
Come inside, my dear.

989
00:36:22,275 --> 00:36:24,344
Oh, it's the Olive Garden.

990
00:36:24,379 --> 00:36:26,000
Yeah, I also hate
it when they seat you

991
00:36:26,034 --> 00:36:27,310
before you get a
look at the menu.

992
00:36:27,344 --> 00:36:28,793
- Yeah.
- Ugh.

993
00:36:29,793 --> 00:36:31,862
So I bought land
on the edge of Mordor,

994
00:36:31,896 --> 00:36:32,758
it's really coming back.

995
00:36:32,793 --> 00:36:34,103
These are the
designs of the prison

996
00:36:34,137 --> 00:36:35,896
towers and passageways.

997
00:36:35,931 --> 00:36:37,000
Thank you, Plop.

998
00:36:38,724 --> 00:36:40,275
Well, I got a party
of eight coming in,

999
00:36:40,310 --> 00:36:41,896
jousting rush just started.

1000
00:36:44,689 --> 00:36:46,517
- Ah, and we're back.
- Wow.

1001
00:36:46,551 --> 00:36:49,000
There's still some
contact, her lips are moving.

1002
00:36:49,034 --> 00:36:50,689
Please get me
out of this film.

1003
00:36:50,724 --> 00:36:51,827
- But there's no speech.
- Please?

1004
00:36:51,862 --> 00:36:53,724
I'll go back to
waitressing, I promise.

1005
00:36:53,758 --> 00:36:56,344
She may be this way
until the end of her life.

1006
00:36:58,448 --> 00:37:01,206
- Which one?
- Witch one, get it?

1007
00:37:01,241 --> 00:37:02,724
- Witch one?
- Kill him.

1008
00:37:02,758 --> 00:37:05,758
[Crow laughs]
It's okay, it's okay.

1009
00:37:05,793 --> 00:37:07,931
- It's Corman. It's Corman.
- I know.

1010
00:37:07,965 --> 00:37:09,586
[Meg Maud cackles]

1011
00:37:09,620 --> 00:37:12,034
Tis a fine brew,
we are finished.

1012
00:37:12,068 --> 00:37:13,034
What will you do with me?

1013
00:37:13,068 --> 00:37:14,413
Who knows, my child?

1014
00:37:14,448 --> 00:37:16,034
Perhaps I'll turn
thee into an owl

1015
00:37:16,068 --> 00:37:17,965
to catch mice for my cauldron.

1016
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:19,137
Then thou art a witch.

1017
00:37:19,172 --> 00:37:21,724
Find one who say Meg
Maud is not a witch.

1018
00:37:21,758 --> 00:37:24,448
And I'll turn
butter out of blood.

1019
00:37:24,482 --> 00:37:26,379
- Yuck.
- I know thee, Helene.

1020
00:37:26,413 --> 00:37:29,241
- Smolkin is my friend.
- Mother, please.

1021
00:37:29,275 --> 00:37:30,724
How did thou escape?

1022
00:37:30,758 --> 00:37:33,448
A voice that was mine
self in ages yet to come

1023
00:37:33,482 --> 00:37:35,275
did show me the way
to loose my bond.

1024
00:37:35,310 --> 00:37:37,620
- Ah!
- Ah, ah, ah.

1025
00:37:38,310 --> 00:37:39,310
By a voice?

1026
00:37:39,344 --> 00:37:41,931
In ages yet to come?

1027
00:37:41,965 --> 00:37:43,103
This is not the sort of magic

1028
00:37:43,137 --> 00:37:45,344
that Satan has given to me.

1029
00:37:45,379 --> 00:37:46,931
Then thou art a witch?

1030
00:37:46,965 --> 00:37:49,137
I was at thy trial.

1031
00:37:49,172 --> 00:37:51,241
I heard the witness Livia swear

1032
00:37:51,275 --> 00:37:55,241
that she did see thee
cast a spell on Smolkin.

1033
00:37:55,275 --> 00:37:57,724
So uh, how do
you like your eggs?

1034
00:37:57,758 --> 00:38:00,724
One last ingredient
for my brew.

1035
00:38:00,758 --> 00:38:01,758
Oh, yeah.

1036
00:38:01,793 --> 00:38:05,655
One raven strand
of maiden virtue.

1037
00:38:05,689 --> 00:38:08,034
It seems like David
Brinkley, "one raven strand"...

1038
00:38:08,068 --> 00:38:10,241
Thou does not
mean to kill me?

1039
00:38:10,275 --> 00:38:12,517
They have named thee witch.

1040
00:38:12,551 --> 00:38:14,482
If I am a witch,
the same as thee,

1041
00:38:14,517 --> 00:38:16,344
should not sister help sister?

1042
00:38:16,379 --> 00:38:17,551
Huh? I didn't get that.

1043
00:38:17,586 --> 00:38:20,034
Aye, aye, that is true.

1044
00:38:20,068 --> 00:38:21,689
We witches must stand together.

1045
00:38:21,724 --> 00:38:23,000
[Meg Maud laughs]

1046
00:38:23,034 --> 00:38:24,275
Good, well said, Helene.

1047
00:38:24,310 --> 00:38:26,551
Perhaps I'll give thee thy head.

1048
00:38:26,586 --> 00:38:28,206
Stay here, little witch,

1049
00:38:28,241 --> 00:38:31,000
and bar the door to all but me.

1050
00:38:32,241 --> 00:38:33,655
I'm going down
to the Winn-Dixie

1051
00:38:33,689 --> 00:38:35,689
for some grease that's sweating
from the murderer's pubic.

1052
00:38:35,724 --> 00:38:38,379
I have some conjouring to do.

1053
00:38:38,413 --> 00:38:40,172
Oh, could you pick
me up some Rice Dream?

1054
00:38:40,206 --> 00:38:42,827
- She's a weirdo, man.
- Mmhmm.

1055
00:38:47,689 --> 00:38:51,758
She's hitting happy hour
with Margaret Hamilton.

1056
00:38:51,793 --> 00:38:54,793
[knocks at door]
Community Theater Witch!

1057
00:38:56,206 --> 00:38:58,551
Must be here for
my Ox Stomach Pudding.

1058
00:39:01,137 --> 00:39:02,379
Now there's a
fine face to see

1059
00:39:02,413 --> 00:39:03,896
on such a fine night!

1060
00:39:03,931 --> 00:39:05,034
Let me in, Scroop.

1061
00:39:05,068 --> 00:39:06,758
You hiring strippers?

1062
00:39:07,379 --> 00:39:08,413
Who else has been here?

1063
00:39:08,448 --> 00:39:10,448
- Helene has escaped.
- Escaped?

1064
00:39:10,482 --> 00:39:11,586
- Escaped!
- Escaped.

1065
00:39:11,620 --> 00:39:12,793
Well, there've
been no soldiers.

1066
00:39:12,827 --> 00:39:15,620
Pendragon is upstairs,
with a maiden, Livia.

1067
00:39:15,655 --> 00:39:17,965
Livia?
Call him down.

1068
00:39:19,172 --> 00:39:21,034
Ho! Pendragon!
[group laughs]

1069
00:39:21,068 --> 00:39:22,137
I coulda done that, jeez!

1070
00:39:22,172 --> 00:39:25,000
Say nothing to Livia,
she must not learn of this.

1071
00:39:25,034 --> 00:39:26,793
Huzzah, who's the babe?

1072
00:39:26,827 --> 00:39:30,793
This is Meg Maud, she has
news of great import for thee.

1073
00:39:30,827 --> 00:39:33,034
Ask nothing, get
thee with all haste

1074
00:39:33,068 --> 00:39:33,482
to my cottage in the marsh.

1075
00:39:33,517 --> 00:39:35,103
And you are...

1076
00:39:35,137 --> 00:39:36,896
It's just beyond the hillock
where they hang the highwaymen.

1077
00:39:36,931 --> 00:39:38,310
What say thee?

1078
00:39:38,344 --> 00:39:40,965
Ask nothing, ride as
thou thy horse had wings!

1079
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:42,448
I trust you implicitly.

1080
00:39:44,310 --> 00:39:46,068
Now I'll go play
with his clothes.

1081
00:39:47,724 --> 00:39:49,724
[cat meows]
[Crow hacks]

1082
00:39:50,620 --> 00:39:52,758
[knocking at door]
I'm shapeshifting.

1083
00:39:52,793 --> 00:39:55,103
The door's
unlatched, pray enter.

1084
00:39:55,137 --> 00:39:57,655
[group singsongs]

1085
00:39:58,862 --> 00:40:01,344
What be thy business
with Pendragon, witch?

1086
00:40:01,379 --> 00:40:03,620
I think that I
shall marry him.

1087
00:40:03,655 --> 00:40:04,206
Ha!

1088
00:40:04,241 --> 00:40:05,379
He would not have thee

1089
00:40:05,413 --> 00:40:07,827
with thy gullet
stuffed with gold.

1090
00:40:07,862 --> 00:40:10,310
- You called me "witch."
- That really hurt.

1091
00:40:10,344 --> 00:40:13,310
No woman, man, or
creature like yourself

1092
00:40:13,344 --> 00:40:14,517
has dared to call me that and--

1093
00:40:14,551 --> 00:40:17,034
Lived to see another, witch?

1094
00:40:17,068 --> 00:40:18,000
I wasn't gonna say that.

1095
00:40:18,034 --> 00:40:19,862
We know one the other well.

1096
00:40:19,896 --> 00:40:23,448
One day, thy mother
did bear a female child.

1097
00:40:23,482 --> 00:40:26,137
And on another day she
did sell her soul to Satan

1098
00:40:26,172 --> 00:40:27,724
and become his bird of prey.

1099
00:40:27,758 --> 00:40:28,931
Oh, so you know about that.

1100
00:40:28,965 --> 00:40:32,137
One day, my mother
bore a female child,

1101
00:40:32,172 --> 00:40:34,586
and she did grow
aged and deformed.

1102
00:40:34,620 --> 00:40:35,827
Is this blank verse?

1103
00:40:35,862 --> 00:40:38,758
And on another day,
she cheated Satan,

1104
00:40:38,793 --> 00:40:41,896
learned his tricks and
yet retained her soul.

1105
00:40:41,931 --> 00:40:42,620
And her water.

1106
00:40:42,655 --> 00:40:44,620
I am thy match, witch,

1107
00:40:44,655 --> 00:40:47,310
but I am not thy kind.

1108
00:40:47,344 --> 00:40:48,620
I know it well.

1109
00:40:48,655 --> 00:40:49,827
You're just mad
that Bobby Russell

1110
00:40:49,862 --> 00:40:52,448
didn't ask you to the ski trip.

1111
00:40:52,482 --> 00:40:55,517
You will make
me a fine opponent.

1112
00:40:55,551 --> 00:40:56,689
What the hell is this,

1113
00:40:56,724 --> 00:40:58,827
a bust of Chiang Kai-shek
made out of liver?

1114
00:41:00,379 --> 00:41:01,586
Ooh!

1115
00:41:02,379 --> 00:41:03,793
- Take care, strumpet!
- Gimme!

1116
00:41:03,827 --> 00:41:07,275
I know thy magic
better than thyself.

1117
00:41:07,310 --> 00:41:13,034
[Mystery Science Theater
3000 theme music]

1118
00:41:13,068 --> 00:41:15,551
Do you get free tailoring
on each suit you buy?

1119
00:41:15,586 --> 00:41:16,931
I guarantee it.

1120
00:41:16,965 --> 00:41:19,103
Is there water at the
bottom of the ocean?

1121
00:41:19,137 --> 00:41:21,034
I guarantee it.

1122
00:41:21,068 --> 00:41:22,068
Do I guarantee it?

1123
00:41:22,103 --> 00:41:23,827
I guarantee it.

1124
00:41:23,862 --> 00:41:25,586
Ah, Crow, you
wanna get going?

1125
00:41:25,620 --> 00:41:26,862
'Cause we're gonna get a
Hot Pocket or something.

1126
00:41:26,896 --> 00:41:28,862
I guar... Oh, sure, great.
Okay, great.

1127
00:41:28,896 --> 00:41:30,896
Fist full of
Philly Beef, for me.

1128
00:41:30,931 --> 00:41:31,689
Whoa!

1129
00:41:31,724 --> 00:41:33,551
Who hath summoned me?

1130
00:41:33,586 --> 00:41:35,241
Well, I, I don't
think that I did.

1131
00:41:35,275 --> 00:41:36,620
Did you guys?

1132
00:41:36,655 --> 00:41:37,793
- I don't think so.
- No, not that I recall.

1133
00:41:37,827 --> 00:41:39,344
Someone has brought me here

1134
00:41:39,379 --> 00:41:41,586
from the realm of the unknown,

1135
00:41:41,620 --> 00:41:43,241
and I intend to, uh oh...

1136
00:41:43,275 --> 00:41:44,862
- Uh oh.
- Whoa.

1137
00:41:46,551 --> 00:41:47,862
Didn't mean to do that.

1138
00:41:48,620 --> 00:41:49,655
Didn't mean to do that.

1139
00:41:49,689 --> 00:41:51,931
Because I have
terrible, dark powers,

1140
00:41:51,965 --> 00:41:53,034
- Sure you do.
- Which I intend to...

1141
00:41:53,068 --> 00:41:54,206
- Yeah.
- Oh, cripes!

1142
00:41:55,275 --> 00:41:57,034
- There you go again.
- What the?

1143
00:41:57,068 --> 00:41:57,896
Oh.

1144
00:41:58,724 --> 00:42:01,000
Oh, never been
a football before.

1145
00:42:01,034 --> 00:42:01,793
That was cool.

1146
00:42:01,827 --> 00:42:03,827
The heck is going on, here?

1147
00:42:03,862 --> 00:42:05,655
Uh, ma'am, do you
need a glass of water?

1148
00:42:05,689 --> 00:42:06,896
- Yeah.
- Yes, you know...

1149
00:42:06,931 --> 00:42:07,758
No, no, I...

1150
00:42:08,482 --> 00:42:10,517
I want your very souls, and I...

1151
00:42:10,551 --> 00:42:11,896
- Oh, wow.
- Oh, boy.

1152
00:42:11,931 --> 00:42:12,931
Oh, oh!

1153
00:42:15,965 --> 00:42:17,689
Oh, penguin? Wow.

1154
00:42:18,413 --> 00:42:19,827
- Trying my best...
- Yeah.

1155
00:42:19,862 --> 00:42:22,241
- Just a little bit rusty...
- Sure, it takes it outta ya.

1156
00:42:22,275 --> 00:42:25,000
- It's just, oh boy!
- Whoa!

1157
00:42:27,862 --> 00:42:28,586
Wah!

1158
00:42:29,379 --> 00:42:30,068
Yikes.

1159
00:42:30,620 --> 00:42:32,689
Uh, ma'am?

1160
00:42:32,724 --> 00:42:34,310
Uh, evil, soul-stealing ma'am?

1161
00:42:34,344 --> 00:42:36,793
Ah, shape-shifting
bride of Satan?

1162
00:42:36,827 --> 00:42:38,344
Uh, Missus Witchiness?

1163
00:42:38,379 --> 00:42:39,689
Oh, darn it.

1164
00:42:39,724 --> 00:42:42,241
I'm stuck, and, I'm stuck!

1165
00:42:42,275 --> 00:42:43,896
Oh, this is so annoying.

1166
00:42:43,931 --> 00:42:45,103
Well, whenever you get--
[klaxon buzzes]

1167
00:42:45,137 --> 00:42:46,482
Movie sign!

1168
00:42:46,517 --> 00:42:49,793
Hey, where are you going...
[voice recedes]

1169
00:42:51,068 --> 00:42:53,103
[chains rattle]

1170
00:42:53,137 --> 00:42:57,275
[gates clang]

1171
00:42:58,793 --> 00:43:00,241
You know, we could
use some bleach.

1172
00:43:00,275 --> 00:43:01,724
Still tonight, Helene.

1173
00:43:01,758 --> 00:43:03,551
Still one deadly night.

1174
00:43:03,586 --> 00:43:05,034
Let's have some soup.

1175
00:43:05,068 --> 00:43:05,620
Where's Meg?

1176
00:43:05,655 --> 00:43:06,275
The witch?

1177
00:43:06,310 --> 00:43:07,310
She's at the bar.

1178
00:43:07,344 --> 00:43:09,413
For she thinks I
am the same as she.

1179
00:43:09,448 --> 00:43:11,034
I fooled her.
[Pendragon laughs]

1180
00:43:11,068 --> 00:43:13,241
You couldn't fool
a child in his cradle.

1181
00:43:13,275 --> 00:43:14,482
Gee, thanks.

1182
00:43:14,517 --> 00:43:15,758
She is the one sent
me here to find you.

1183
00:43:15,793 --> 00:43:17,103
Why'd you ask where she is?

1184
00:43:17,137 --> 00:43:18,724
I'm glad of that.

1185
00:43:18,758 --> 00:43:21,448
And yet, Pendragon, this
place, 'tis unhealthy.

1186
00:43:21,482 --> 00:43:22,689
I sense radon.

1187
00:43:22,724 --> 00:43:25,758
Well come, then, I'll
take you to the tavern.

1188
00:43:25,793 --> 00:43:27,689
Scroop is a good fellow.

1189
00:43:27,724 --> 00:43:30,206
He'll help watch
over you, come on.

1190
00:43:30,241 --> 00:43:32,413
We'll get a burger basket
and a couple of lineys.

1191
00:43:32,448 --> 00:43:36,793
So, you would
enchant Pendragon as
you did poor Smolkin.

1192
00:43:36,827 --> 00:43:38,931
We shall see, my dear.

1193
00:43:38,965 --> 00:43:40,448
So we shall.

1194
00:43:40,482 --> 00:43:42,551
Helene lives but
a few more hours.

1195
00:43:42,586 --> 00:43:44,241
Then Pendragon is mine.

1196
00:43:44,275 --> 00:43:47,034
- I'll take that challenge.
- And your little dog, too.

1197
00:43:47,068 --> 00:43:47,620
Hark you this:

1198
00:43:48,586 --> 00:43:50,724
Pendragon shall be
free of thee forever.

1199
00:43:50,758 --> 00:43:53,482
And what's more,
the maid condemed

1200
00:43:53,517 --> 00:43:54,965
shall live beyond this night,

1201
00:43:55,000 --> 00:43:57,896
and live to see
thee to thy death.

1202
00:43:57,931 --> 00:43:59,068
Says you!

1203
00:43:59,103 --> 00:44:02,241
Is it a wager, then, my
twisted copy of a wizardess?

1204
00:44:02,275 --> 00:44:05,793
Try every trick you
know, I'll vanquish thee.

1205
00:44:05,827 --> 00:44:07,827
And I'll do it in my sleep.

1206
00:44:07,862 --> 00:44:09,275
- You got me.
- Sleep?

1207
00:44:09,310 --> 00:44:11,068
Not while I'm awake.

1208
00:44:11,896 --> 00:44:14,000
Aye, sleep is coming.

1209
00:44:14,655 --> 00:44:16,758
In the sulphurous pit!

1210
00:44:16,793 --> 00:44:18,793
You mean Scroop's underarm?

1211
00:44:18,827 --> 00:44:20,206
Oh, she's good,
she nailed me there.

1212
00:44:20,241 --> 00:44:22,137
Whew. Zing.

1213
00:44:25,620 --> 00:44:27,931
Now I understand
dwarf-tossing.

1214
00:44:28,827 --> 00:44:30,896
Good, old fashioned
nightmare fuel.

1215
00:44:32,689 --> 00:44:35,172
You know, this forest
could use a plant.

1216
00:44:36,931 --> 00:44:39,758
This kingdom has
maybe six people.

1217
00:44:41,724 --> 00:44:44,344
♪ Me in White Satin
[Mike chuckles]

1218
00:44:44,379 --> 00:44:45,689
Sorry.

1219
00:44:46,689 --> 00:44:48,965
There goes the dumbest
knight in the realm.

1220
00:44:51,103 --> 00:44:53,103
Let us now fly to
Smolkin's church yard,

1221
00:44:53,137 --> 00:44:54,655
and there prepare
the tables of earth

1222
00:44:54,689 --> 00:44:56,379
for the banquet of the Sabbath.

1223
00:44:57,482 --> 00:44:59,517
Let us be little B-1 Bombers.

1224
00:44:59,551 --> 00:45:01,413
[Smokin sings]
Ah, jeez.

1225
00:45:01,448 --> 00:45:03,206
- Oh, man.
- Do you have a gun?

1226
00:45:05,551 --> 00:45:06,896
[Crow imitates Smolkin singing]

1227
00:45:06,931 --> 00:45:10,655
♪ She tried, but the
corpse sadly cried

1228
00:45:10,689 --> 00:45:11,827
Reconnaissance!

1229
00:45:11,862 --> 00:45:14,344
Be off, ghoul,
and leave me alone.

1230
00:45:14,379 --> 00:45:16,000
The first highway worker.

1231
00:45:16,896 --> 00:45:18,206
Good evening, Smolkin.

1232
00:45:18,241 --> 00:45:19,379
From a Sara!

1233
00:45:19,413 --> 00:45:21,310
Ah, 'tis Livia, the witch.

1234
00:45:21,344 --> 00:45:23,689
Welcome to my flesh farm.

1235
00:45:23,724 --> 00:45:25,379
Disturb me not, lummox.

1236
00:45:25,413 --> 00:45:27,379
I must hasten to sweep
these wandering ghosts back

1237
00:45:27,413 --> 00:45:30,068
to their earthen homes before
the witch's Sabbath begins.

1238
00:45:30,103 --> 00:45:32,896
Oh, and are you to
be the Queen of Sorcery

1239
00:45:32,931 --> 00:45:34,620
at the revelry tonight, Livia?

1240
00:45:34,655 --> 00:45:37,103
Aye, and stand at
Lucifer's right hand.

1241
00:45:37,137 --> 00:45:38,758
- Cool.
- 'Tis said the queen

1242
00:45:38,793 --> 00:45:41,793
must bring to Satan's hand
one freshly severed head

1243
00:45:41,827 --> 00:45:44,793
as proof that she is
true to his black trust.

1244
00:45:44,827 --> 00:45:47,689
A head. I never got...

1245
00:45:47,724 --> 00:45:48,931
- Take Smolkins'!
- Yeah!

1246
00:45:48,965 --> 00:45:50,137
- Get him, get his head!
- Say I cut yours off?

1247
00:45:50,172 --> 00:45:51,448
- The head of a madman,
- Yeah, let's do it!

1248
00:45:51,482 --> 00:45:53,000
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

1249
00:45:53,793 --> 00:45:54,862
The devil might feel slighted

1250
00:45:54,896 --> 00:45:56,724
if you brought him
less than the best.

1251
00:45:56,758 --> 00:45:57,896
He's not that picky.

1252
00:45:57,931 --> 00:46:00,793
Pity, thou must
seek elsewhere.

1253
00:46:00,827 --> 00:46:03,793
I must hurry home to
see how fare my charges.

1254
00:46:03,827 --> 00:46:05,965
He's violating
a lot of fire laws.

1255
00:46:07,689 --> 00:46:10,103
They mustn't
know of our love.

1256
00:46:10,137 --> 00:46:12,586
I have the urge to pour
Frangelico out of his neck.

1257
